        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: require exact claims for direct cloud cleanup",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- require canonical lease IDs before DigitalOcean, Linode, Vultr, or Scaleway resources enter Crabbox inventory\n- require exact provider/account-or-project/resource-bound local claims before reuse, stop, status-touch, or cleanup\n- skip claimless or mismatched cleanup candidates without aborting cleanup of later exactly claimed resources\n- keep claimless canonical resources read-only until explicit `--reclaim` adoption; never synthesize destructive ownership from remote tags\n- preserve interrupted-create recovery while validating exact provider identity\n- restrict key-only or cloudless rollback Scaleway and Vultr recovery claims to identityless cleanup; they cannot authorize live server deletion\n- keep read-only resolve paths from writing claims\n- document the ownership boundary in provider and stop documentation\n\nCloses https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/811\n\n## Verification\n\nCurrent candidate: `a7718e92a5db3c92a33614fb489b35da4390efd9`.\n\n- `go test -race ./internal/cli ./internal/providers/digitalocean ./internal/providers/linode ./internal/providers/vultr ./internal/providers/scaleway -count=1`\n- `go test -race ./internal/providers/shared ./internal/providers/digitalocean ./internal/providers/linode ./internal/providers/vultr ./internal/providers/scaleway -count=1`\n- `go test -race ./internal/cli -run TestControllerExpiryTransitionCancelsActiveWarmup -count=10`\n- `go vet ./internal/cli ./internal/providers/digitalocean ./internal/providers/linode ./internal/providers/vultr ./internal/providers/scaleway`\n- `scripts/check-docs.sh`\n- Rebased onto the W&B and RunPod ownership mainline plus the pure-Go Apple VM helper; conflicts were limited to composing 0.35.1 changelog entries. Affected provider race tests, vet, docs, diff checks, and the warning-free CLI build pass.\n- Full branch autoreview clean; focused key-only Vultr recovery autoreview clean (0.86); cleanup continuation autoreview clean (0.78); live-account cleanup preflight autoreview clean (0.83).\n- Cleanup preflight now resolves current DigitalOcean, Linode, and Vultr account identity before authorizing deletion, fills only missing inventory identity, and skips stale-account claims without aborting later eligible cleanup.\n- All inline review findings are fixed, answered, and resolved.\n\n## Provider-live proof\n\n- DigitalOcean at `9d074c70`: create, status --wait, run, list, stop, empty inventory; lease `cbx_41ac9aa551b8`.\n- Linode at `9d074c70`: create, status --wait, run, list, stop, empty inventory; lease `cbx_fed152b988e2`.\n- Scaleway at `ee82a6fb`: create, status --wait, run, list, stop, empty inventory; lease `cbx_f91178ad1c09`.\n- Vultr: pending because no authenticated API credential is available after targeted environment and approved 1Password lookup.\n\nThe later commits add provider-identity validation and claim-safe cleanup control flow; they do not weaken the proven DigitalOcean, Linode, or Scaleway ownership paths.\n\nKeep this PR unmerged until exact-head Vultr create/use/status-touch/stop/empty-inventory proof passes, or that provider-specific gate is explicitly waived.\n\n## Compatibility decision\n\nAccepted fail-closed behavior: claimless, provider-identity-mismatched, or recovery-ambiguous resources remain inspectable but cannot be touched or deleted until explicit reclaim establishes an exact claim.\n",
